# Daggerfall N per-frame log -- one line per PRESENTED frame.
# No readback, no settle, no cooldown: this instrument cannot
# quiet the thing it is pointed at. Between-frames motion is
# arithmetic on adjacent lines.
# frame dt_ms game_s speed fov_y eye_x eye_y eye_z yaw pitch
# DECIMATED 1:10 from the raw DFN_FRAME_LOG (the run presented ~1150 frames/s,
# so this keeps ~115 samples per second against a 60 Hz simulation tick --
# every tick is still sampled about twice, and the quantity claimed from this
# file is a SUSTAINED DISPLACEMENT (mm of eye travel) plus the SHAPE of a
# 0.15 s ramp, neither of which decimation can hide. It is NOT a per-frame
# meander like docs/FINDING_RUN_SMEAR.md, where every frame had to be kept.
